%% How a question becomes an answer.
%% Notes span two participants so their text is not clipped.
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor U as Browser
  participant ALB as Load Balancer
  participant API as FastAPI on Fargate
  participant BR as Titan Embed v2
  participant OS as OpenSearch
  participant LLM as Nova Lite

  U->>ALB: GET /
  ALB->>API: forward to task :8000
  API-->>U: index.html, no credentials in the page

  U->>ALB: POST /query {question, k, mode}
  ALB->>API: forward

  Note over API,OS: No x-api-key needed: require_auth is false.<br/>Every AWS call below is SigV4 signed by the task role.

  API->>BR: embed question, 1024 dims, normalized
  BR-->>API: query vector

  par Two retrievers, same index
    API->>OS: kNN on vector field, size k*2
    OS-->>API: passages ranked by cosine similarity
  and
    API->>OS: BM25 match on text field, size k*2
    OS-->>API: passages ranked by keyword score
  end

  Note over API,OS: Cosine and BM25 scores are not comparable,<br/>so fusion uses rank only: sum of 1/(60 + rank).<br/>Passages both retrievers rank highly win.

  API->>API: reciprocal rank fusion, keep top k
  API->>API: number the passages, cap context at 12000 chars

  alt Nothing retrieved
    API-->>U: "could not find anything relevant"
    Note over API,LLM: The model is never called with empty context,<br/>which would invite an ungrounded answer.
  else Passages found
    API->>LLM: Converse API, system prompt + context + question, temperature 0
    LLM-->>API: answer citing [1] [2]
    API-->>ALB: {answer, citations[], model_id}
    ALB-->>U: JSON, rendered with its sources
  end
